 "actionbar_contextmenu_text": "Text",
 "actionbar_lenshelp": "<p>Every player can have several action bars with 50 action buttons per bar. For every hotkey preset, players can configure separate action bars. By right-clicking on an action button, you will have different options depending whether you like to assign a spell, an object or a text, or if you like to assign a hotkey to an action button.</p>\n<p>Action buttons which are already in use have the additional option \"Clear Action\" which will delete an assigned action from this button. Action buttons are greyed out if they contain an object which you do not have with you or a spell which your character cannot use.</p>\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <td><img src='/images/lenshelp-icon-locked.png'><img src='/images/lenshelp-icon-unlocked.png'></td>\n    <td>If the lock is open, you can easily assign or switch an action to an action button using \"drag&drop\". Hotkeys are bound to an action button, so they will not be moved this way. Close the lock to avoid unintentional moving of actions, for example when hunting. If locked, you cannot assign any actions by \"drag&drop\" but still via the context menu.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><img src='/images/lenshelp-icon-arrow-left.png'><img src='/images/lenshelp-icon-arrow-right.png'></td>\n    <td>Go to the next/previous action button.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><img src='/images/lenshelp-icon-arrowskip-left.png'><img src='/images/lenshelp-icon-arrowskip-right.png'></td>\n    <td>Go to the last/first action button.</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n<p>Finally, in the Options menu \"Action Bars\", you have several options to adjust your action bars. For a detailed description on how to assign actions to action buttons, please take a look at the manual.</p>\n          ",
